{"seconds": 29.3, "exit": 0, "final": "After Rf3+ Ke7 Rxf7+, White wins. Now let me confirm the clearest line is Rf3+ winning the queen:\n\n**Best move:** Rf3+\n\n**Main line:** Rf3+ Ke5 (or Ke7) Rxf2, and White is up a queen (9 points). Black's best try Bf5 doesn't help: after Rxf2, White is still winning easily.\n\n**Motif:** fork (the rook checks the king and attacks the queen simultaneously)\n\n**Coaching explanation:**\n\nWhen your opponent's queen is loose (undefended), look for ways to attack it while creating a bigger threat. Here, Rf3+ is a royal fork\u2014it checks the Black king on f6 and simultaneously attacks the undefended queen on f2. Black must move the king, and then you capture the queen with Rxf2, winning 9 points of material. This pattern\u2014a check that also attacks an undefended piece\u2014is one of the strongest tactical motifs to spot.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Rf3+\", \"line\": [\"Rf3+\", \"Ke5\", \"Rxf2\"], \"motifs\": [\"fork\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "B7/p4p1p/4bk2/2p5/8/6R1/P4q2/6RK w - - 0 31"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "B7/p4p1p/4bk2/2p5/8/6R1/P4q2/6RK w - - 0 31"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "B7/p4p1p/4bk2/2p5/8/6R1/P4q2/6RK w - - 0 31", "square": "f2"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "B7/p4p1p/4bk2/2p5/8/6R1/P4q2/6RK w - - 0 31", "square": "f6"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "B7/p4p1p/4bk2/2p5/8/6R1/P4q2/6RK w - - 0 31", "square": "e6"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "B7/p4p1p/4bk2/2p5/8/6R1/P4q2/6RK w - - 0 31", "square": "a8"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "B7/p4p1p/4bk2/2p5/8/6R1/P4q2/6RK w - - 0 31", "square": "g3"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "B7/p4p1p/4bk2/2p5/8/6R1/P4q2/6RK w - - 0 31", "square": "g1"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "B7/p4p1p/4bk2/2p5/8/6R1/P4q